    <!-- 1. WHAT THIS IS -->
    <h2 id="what-this-is">1. What This Is</h2>

    <p>This is not a blog. It's a premium editorial publishing system designed to grow high-quality search traffic, capture email subscribers, support affiliate monetization, and qualify for premium ad monetization (Mediavine at 50K monthly sessions).</p>

    <p>Think of it as a hybrid of:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>An elegant lifestyle magazine with a real editorial voice</li>
      <li>A practical, search-first editorial site that ranks for the queries people actually type</li>
      <li>An affiliate-friendly recommendation engine with tasteful, embedded commerce</li>
      <li>A newsletter-driven personal brand platform</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>What it's built to do</h3>
    <ol>
      <li>Increase qualified organic traffic through crawlable topic architecture</li>
      <li>Improve the number of rankable entry pages across restaurants, travel, hotels, style, and recipes</li>
      <li>Capture email subscribers through editorial CTAs that feel native, not desperate</li>
      <li>Add affiliate, booking, and reservation monetization before premium ads kick in</li>
      <li>Build reusable systems so new content compounds instead of existing as isolated posts</li>
    </ol>

    <h3>What it's not</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>A generic blog with flat archives and no structure</li>
      <li>A content farm flooding pages with AI filler</li>
      <li>An over-engineered SaaS tool that needs a developer to publish a post</li>
    </ul>

    <hr style="border: none; border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); margin: 3rem 0;" />

    <!-- 2. ARCHITECTURE -->
    <h2 id="architecture">2. Technical Architecture</h2>

    <p>Your magazine lives at <strong>cafecito-ai.com/magazine</strong>. Here's how it works under the hood.</p>

    <h3>Stack</h3>
    <table class="admin-table" style="margin: 1.5rem 0 2rem;">
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><strong>Framework</strong></td><td>Astro 5.x — static site generator. Every page is pre-rendered HTML.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Hosting</strong></td><td>Cloudflare Workers + KV storage. Global CDN, edge-cached, near-instant loads.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Content</strong></td><td>Markdown files with YAML frontmatter. No database. Files live in <code>src/content/posts/</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>CMS</strong></td><td>File-based. Edit markdown directly, or use the growth engine CLI to generate drafts.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Styling</strong></td><td>Single <code>global.css</code>. No CSS framework. Custom editorial design.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>JavaScript</strong></td><td>Minimal. Only for nav toggle, scroll behavior, and analytics events. No JS frameworks.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Growth Engine</strong></td><td>Separate Node.js CLI (<code>aileen</code> command) for AI-assisted content creation.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h3>Why this matters</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Every page is static HTML</strong> — Google sees exactly what readers see. No client-side rendering hiding content.</li>
      <li><strong>Metadata is in the initial HTML</strong> — titles, descriptions, Open Graph, structured data all render server-side.</li>
      <li><strong>No blocking third-party JavaScript</strong> — article pages load fast. Analytics loads async.</li>
      <li><strong>Edge-cached globally</strong> — pages serve from the Cloudflare node closest to the reader.</li>
      <li><strong>Small bundle</strong> — no React, no Vue, no framework JS. Just content.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Rendering and crawlability</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>All content pages are prerendered HTML (SSG)</li>
      <li>H1, intro copy, internal links, and category links are present in HTML output</li>
      <li>Canonical URLs are deterministic on every page</li>
      <li>XML sitemap auto-generates at build time</li>
      <li>Robots.txt is explicit</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Performance targets</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Responsive images with lazy loading for below-the-fold media</li>
      <li>Minimal layout shift (no JavaScript-dependent content)</li>
      <li>Preconnected font strategy (Google Fonts with <code>preconnect</code>)</li>
      <li>Article body width capped at 680px for comfortable reading</li>
      <li>Template rhythm designed to accommodate future ad insertion without layout breakage</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Build &amp; deploy</h3>
    <p>One command to build, one command to deploy:</p>
    <pre><code>npm run build        # Builds all pages to dist/
npx wrangler deploy  # Pushes to Cloudflare</code></pre>
    <p>Or use the growth engine shortcut: <code>aileen publish</code></p>

    <hr style="border: none; border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); margin: 3rem 0;" />

    <!-- 3. INFORMATION ARCHITECTURE -->
    <h2 id="information-architecture">3. Information Architecture</h2>

    <p>The site replaces a shallow blog model with a true editorial information architecture — sections with intent, destination taxonomy, and content types that serve different search queries.</p>

    <h3>Primary navigation</h3>
    <table class="admin-table" style="margin: 1.5rem 0 2rem;">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Section</th><th>URL</th><th>Intent</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><a href={`${base}/travel/`}>Travel</a></td><td>/magazine/travel/</td><td>Destination guides, itineraries, where-to-eat and where-to-stay roundups</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href={`${base}/style/`}>Style</a></td><td>/magazine/style/</td><td>Quiet luxury, capsule wardrobes, outfit guides, seasonal edits</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href={`${base}/recipes/`}>Recipes</a></td><td>/magazine/recipes/</td><td>Signature recipes, weeknight staples, dinner party menus</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href={`${base}/lifestyle/`}>Lifestyle</a></td><td>/magazine/lifestyle/</td><td>Intentional living, morning routines, home aesthetics</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href={`${base}/destinations/`}>Destinations</a></td><td>/magazine/destinations/</td><td>City hub pages aggregating cross-category content</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href={`${base}/about/`}>About</a></td><td>/magazine/about/</td><td>Who you are. Trust signals for readers and Google.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h3>Section intent</h3>

    <p><strong>Travel</strong> covers search-led destination and restaurant guides. Page types: best restaurants in [city], travel guide for [destination], weekend itinerary, things to do, seasonal guides. Also hotel reviews and where-to-stay roundups.</p>

    <p><strong>Style</strong> covers search-friendly but editorial fashion content. Page types: what to wear in [destination] in [season], quiet luxury brands, capsule wardrobe guides, dinner outfit guides, travel outfit edits, style icon breakdowns.</p>

    <p><strong>Recipes</strong> covers narrow, high-quality recipe-markup-enabled utility content. Signature recipes, practical family staples, repeatable kitchen winners. Every recipe gets Recipe structured data.</p>

    <p><strong>Lifestyle</strong> covers editorial lifestyle content. Intentional living, morning routines, home aesthetics, personal essays, trend commentary.</p>

    <h3>Destination taxonomy</h3>

    <p>Destinations are a first-class taxonomy separate from category. A post about "best restaurants in Miami" is a <em>restaurant guide</em> (content type) in the <em>travel</em> pillar tagged with the <em>Miami</em> destination. The Miami destination hub then aggregates restaurant guides, hotel reviews, travel guides, and style guides for that city — all in one page.</p>

    <p>Current destinations:</p>
    <table class="admin-table" style="margin: 1.5rem 0 2rem;">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Destination</th><th>Hub URL</th><th>Hub Page Sections</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><a href={`${base}/destinations/miami/`}>Miami</a></td><td>/magazine/destinations/miami/</td><td>Where to Eat, Where to Stay, Travel Guides, What to Wear</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href={`${base}/destinations/palm-beach/`}>Palm Beach</a></td><td>/magazine/destinations/palm-beach/</td><td>Same structure, fills as content is published</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href={`${base}/destinations/boston/`}>Boston</a></td><td>/magazine/destinations/boston/</td><td>Same</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href={`${base}/destinations/nyc/`}>NYC</a></td><td>/magazine/destinations/nyc/</td><td>Same</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href={`${base}/destinations/maine/`}>Maine</a></td><td>/magazine/destinations/maine/</td><td>Same</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href={`${base}/destinations/aspen/`}>Aspen</a></td><td>/magazine/destinations/aspen/</td><td>Same</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <p>Each hub page includes: hero image, editorial intro, featured guides, Where to Eat, Where to Stay, What to Wear, Travel Guides, and a newsletter CTA. As you tag more posts with a destination, the hub populates itself automatically.</p>

    <h3>Category pages</h3>
    <p>Each category page (Travel, Style, Recipes, Lifestyle) is a real landing page with editorial intro copy, a hero area, and a post grid — not a raw archive. These pages have their own SEO titles and meta descriptions so they can rank for broad category queries.</p>

    <hr style="border: none; border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); margin: 3rem 0;" />

    <!-- 4. URL STRUCTURE -->
    <h2 id="url-structure">4. URL Structure</h2>

    <p>Clean, human-readable, no date-based cruft.</p>

    <table class="admin-table" style="margin: 1.5rem 0 2rem;">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Pattern</th><th>Example</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Homepage</td><td><code>/magazine/</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Category page</td><td><code>/magazine/travel/</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Post</td><td><code>/magazine/travel/best-restaurants-miami/</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Destination hub</td><td><code>/magazine/destinations/miami/</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Destinations index</td><td><code>/magazine/destinations/</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>About</td><td><code>/magazine/about/</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Admin dashboards</td><td><code>/magazine/admin/</code>, <code>/admin/seo/</code>, etc.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h3>URL rules</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Slugs are human-readable: <code>best-restaurants-miami</code>, not <code>post-12345</code></li>
      <li>No date segments in URLs — content stays evergreen</li>
      <li>No nested category/subcategory cruft</li>
      <li>Posts live under their pillar: <code>/magazine/[pillar]/[slug]/</code></li>
      <li>Trailing slashes are consistent</li>
    </ul>

    <hr style="border: none; border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); margin: 3rem 0;" />

    <!-- 5. CONTENT MODELS -->
    <h2 id="content-models">5. Content Models</h2>

    <p>Every post is a markdown file with YAML frontmatter. The schema is enforced at build time — if required fields are missing or invalid, the build fails and tells you exactly what's wrong.</p>

    <h3>Core fields (required on every post)</h3>
    <table class="admin-table" style="margin: 1.5rem 0 2rem;">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>What It Does</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>title</code></td><td>String</td><td>H1 headline and browser tab title</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>metaDescription</code></td><td>String</td><td>Google search snippet (150-160 chars ideal)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>targetKeyword</code></td><td>String</td><td>Primary SEO keyword. Used by audit tools.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>pillar</code></td><td>travel | style | recipes | lifestyle</td><td>Which category the post belongs to</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>date</code></td><td>String (YYYY-MM-DD)</td><td>Publish date. Used for sorting and schema.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>image</code></td><td>URL</td><td>Hero image. Used in cards, OG tags, schema.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>imageAlt</code></td><td>String</td><td>Alt text for the hero image (SEO + accessibility)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>excerpt</code></td><td>String</td><td>Card text and dek/intro summary</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h3>Content type (defaults to "article")</h3>
    <table class="admin-table" style="margin: 1.5rem 0 2rem;">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Content Type</th><th>When to Use</th><th>Special Features</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>restaurant-guide</code></td><td>Best restaurants in [city], dining roundups</td><td>Reservation CTAs, destination tagging</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>hotel-review</code></td><td>Where to stay guides, hotel roundups</td><td>Booking CTAs, destination tagging</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>travel-guide</code></td><td>City guides, itineraries, things to do</td><td>Booking + reservation + affiliate CTAs</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>style-guide</code></td><td>What to wear, capsule wardrobes, brand edits</td><td>Product grid with affiliate links</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>recipe</code></td><td>Recipes with full instructions</td><td>Recipe JSON-LD schema, cookware affiliate links</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>the-edit</code></td><td>Curated shopping roundups, product picks</td><td>Product grid, heavy affiliate</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>article</code></td><td>General editorial, lifestyle, trends</td><td>Standard template</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>destination-hub</code></td><td>City overview pages</td><td>Auto-aggregates by destination tag</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h3>Optional fields</h3>
    <table class="admin-table" style="margin: 1.5rem 0 2rem;">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>What It Does</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>contentType</code></td><td>Enum (see above)</td><td>Controls template behavior and voice conditioning</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>updatedDate</code></td><td>String (YYYY-MM-DD)</td><td>Shows "Updated" date on the post + <code>dateModified</code> in schema</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>author</code></td><td>String</td><td>Defaults to "Aileen Lavin"</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>draft</code></td><td>Boolean</td><td>If <code>true</code>, the post is excluded from all pages and the sitemap</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>featured</code></td><td>Boolean</td><td>If <code>true</code>, the post appears in the homepage hero</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>featuredOrder</code></td><td>Number</td><td>Controls order among multiple featured posts</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>destinations</code></td><td>Array of strings</td><td>Tags the post for destination hubs: <code>["miami"]</code>, <code>["boston", "maine"]</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>toc</code></td><td>Boolean</td><td>If <code>true</code>, shows an auto-generated Table of Contents from H2 headings</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>affiliateDisclosure</code></td><td>Boolean</td><td>If <code>true</code>, shows FTC-compliant affiliate disclosure at the top</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>relatedPosts</code></td><td>Array of slugs</td><td>Manual override for related content (otherwise auto-resolved)</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h3>Monetization fields</h3>
    <table class="admin-table" style="margin: 1.5rem 0 2rem;">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>What It Renders</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>products</code></td><td>Array of objects</td><td>"Shop the Edit" product grid with name, brand, price, URL, image</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>bookingLinks</code></td><td>Array of objects</td><td>Hotel booking CTA buttons with name, platform, URL</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>reservationLinks</code></td><td>Array of objects</td><td>Restaurant reservation CTA buttons with name, platform, URL</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h3>Tracking fields (managed by growth engine)</h3>
    <table class="admin-table" style="margin: 1.5rem 0 2rem;">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Field</th><th>What It Tracks</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>voiceScore</code></td><td>Voice validator score (0-100) from last check</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>seoScore</code></td><td>SEO audit score from last audit</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>pinsGenerated</code></td><td>Number of Pinterest pin variations created</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>newsletterIncluded</code></td><td>Whether this post has been included in a newsletter</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h3>FAQ field</h3>
    <p>Add an <code>faq</code> array for FAQ sections with structured data. Each entry has a <code>question</code> and <code>answer</code>. This renders a styled FAQ section with FAQPage JSON-LD schema — which gives you a shot at Google featured snippets.</p>
    <pre><code>faq:
  - question: "What are the best restaurants in Miami?"
    answer: "The best restaurants in Miami include..."
  - question: "Do I need reservations?"
    answer: "For most restaurants on this list, yes."</code></pre>

    <h3>Example frontmatter (restaurant guide)</h3>
    <pre><code>---
title: "Best Restaurants in Miami (A Local's Guide for 2026)"
metaDescription: "The best restaurants in Miami — from Aventura to Brickell."
targetKeyword: "best restaurants in miami"
pillar: "travel"
contentType: "restaurant-guide"
date: "2026-03-05"
image: "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-..."
imageAlt: "Elegant restaurant interior with warm lighting"
excerpt: "A local's guide to Miami dining worth the reservation."
draft: false
featured: true
featuredOrder: 1
destinations: ["miami"]
toc: true
affiliateDisclosure: false
faq:
  - question: "What are the best restaurants in Miami?"
    answer: "Daniel's Steakhouse, Makoto, Sunny's..."
reservationLinks:
  - name: "Makoto"
    platform: "Resy"
    url: "https://resy.com/cities/mia/makoto"
---</code></pre>

    <hr style="border: none; border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); margin: 3rem 0;" />

    <!-- 6. PAGE TEMPLATES -->
    <h2 id="page-templates">6. Page Templates</h2>

    <h3>Homepage (<code>/magazine/</code>)</h3>
    <p>Features a hero section with positioning copy, a featured post hero card, and a "Worth Your Time" grid of latest posts. The featured post is controlled by the <code>featured: true</code> frontmatter flag. The homepage drives readers into evergreen clusters, not just the newest posts.</p>

    <h3>Category pages (<code>/magazine/travel/</code>, etc.)</h3>
    <p>Each category page is a real landing page with editorial intro copy, a hero area with the pillar's positioning statement, and a post grid. These have their own SEO titles and meta descriptions so they can rank for broad queries like "luxury travel guides" or "elegant recipes."</p>

    <h3>Article template (<code>/magazine/[pillar]/[slug]/</code>)</h3>
    <p>The article template renders every post. Modules in order:</p>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Breadcrumb</strong> — Home &gt; Pillar &gt; Post title (with BreadcrumbList JSON-LD)</li>
      <li><strong>Content type label</strong> — "Restaurant Guide", "Travel Guide", "Style Guide", etc.</li>
      <li><strong>H1 headline</strong></li>
      <li><strong>Meta line</strong> — Author, date, updated date, reading time</li>
      <li><strong>Destination links</strong> — If tagged, links to destination hub pages</li>
      <li><strong>Hero image</strong> — Full-width with alt text</li>
      <li><strong>Affiliate disclosure</strong> — If <code>affiliateDisclosure: true</code></li>
      <li><strong>Table of contents</strong> — If <code>toc: true</code>, auto-generated from H2 headings</li>
      <li><strong>Body content</strong> — Your markdown, rendered to HTML</li>
      <li><strong>Product grid</strong> — If <code>products</code> array is populated</li>
      <li><strong>Booking CTAs</strong> — If <code>bookingLinks</code> array is populated</li>
      <li><strong>Reservation CTAs</strong> — If <code>reservationLinks</code> array is populated</li>
      <li><strong>FAQ section</strong> — If <code>faq</code> array is populated (with FAQPage JSON-LD)</li>
      <li><strong>Share bar</strong> — Pinterest, email, copy link</li>
      <li><strong>Related posts</strong> — 2 same-pillar + 1 cross-pillar, prefers same-destination</li>
    </ol>

    <h3>Destination hub (<code>/magazine/destinations/[city]/</code>)</h3>
    <p>Each hub has a hero image with editorial intro, then sections: Where to Eat (restaurant guides), Where to Stay (hotel reviews), Travel Guides, What to Wear (style guides), and More (everything else). Sections only appear when there's content to show. Empty hubs show "Guides coming soon."</p>

    <h3>Destinations index (<code>/magazine/destinations/</code>)</h3>
    <p>Shows all destination hubs as cards with post counts, so readers can browse by city.</p>

    <h3>About page (<code>/magazine/about/</code>)</h3>
    <p>Your editorial bio, trust signals, and positioning. Important for E-E-A-T (Google's quality signals).</p>

    <hr style="border: none; border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); margin: 3rem 0;" />

    <!-- 7. COMPONENTS -->
    <h2 id="components">7. Component Library</h2>

    <p>Reusable UI components that maintain consistency across every page:</p>

    <table class="admin-table" style="margin: 1.5rem 0 2rem;">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Component</th><th>File</th><th>What It Does</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><strong>PostCard</strong></td><td><code>PostCard.astro</code></td><td>Article card with image, pillar badge, title, excerpt, date. Used in all grids.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>PostGrid</strong></td><td><code>PostGrid.astro</code></td><td>Responsive grid wrapper for PostCards. Used on category and destination pages.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Breadcrumbs</strong></td><td><code>Breadcrumbs.astro</code></td><td>Home &gt; Pillar &gt; Title breadcrumb navigation for SEO and UX.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>FAQ</strong></td><td><code>FAQ.astro</code></td><td>FAQ section with FAQPage JSON-LD schema markup.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>ProductGrid</strong></td><td><code>ProductGrid.astro</code></td><td>"Shop the Edit" section with product cards showing brand, price, and affiliate links.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>BookingCTA</strong></td><td><code>BookingCTA.astro</code></td><td>Hotel booking call-to-action buttons with platform badges.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>ReservationCTA</strong></td><td><code>ReservationCTA.astro</code></td><td>Restaurant reservation call-to-action buttons with platform badges.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>AffiliateDisclosure</strong></td><td><code>AffiliateDisclosure.astro</code></td><td>FTC-compliant disclosure block placed above the fold when needed.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>TableOfContents</strong></td><td><code>TableOfContents.astro</code></td><td>Auto-generated from H2 headings. Helps readers scan long guides.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>ShareBar</strong></td><td><code>ShareBar.astro</code></td><td>Pinterest save, email, and copy-link buttons with clipboard integration.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

