    <!-- 8. INTERNAL LINKING -->
    <h2 id="internal-linking">8. Internal Linking System</h2>

    <p>Internal linking is a core part of SEO. Every article needs to link to other articles so Google can discover and evaluate your content clusters.</p>

    <h3>Automatic related content</h3>
    <p>Every article shows a "More Worth Your Time" section at the bottom with 3 related posts, automatically resolved:</p>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>2 same-pillar posts</strong> — prefers posts sharing the same destination</li>
      <li><strong>1 cross-pillar post</strong> — creates bridges between content clusters</li>
    </ol>
    <p>You can override this with the <code>relatedPosts</code> frontmatter array for editorial control.</p>

    <h3>Destination hub linking</h3>
    <p>When a post has <code>destinations: ["miami"]</code>, it appears on the Miami hub and the post header links back to the hub. This creates two-way linking between posts and their destination clusters.</p>

    <h3>In-body linking</h3>
    <p>Within the markdown body of each post, include manual links to related content. The build spec calls for at minimum:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>2 related articles in the same category</li>
      <li>1 destination page if the post is destination-specific</li>
      <li>1 adjacent-cluster page where relevant (e.g., a restaurant guide links to the hotel guide for the same city)</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Persistent navigation links</h3>
    <p>The footer links to all pillars, destinations, and the most popular guides — creating persistent internal links on every page.</p>

    <hr style="border: none; border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); margin: 3rem 0;" />

    <!-- 9. SEO -->
    <h2 id="seo">9. SEO Infrastructure</h2>

    <p>SEO isn't a plugin. It's built into every layer of the site.</p>

    <h3>On-page SEO</h3>
    <p>Every page has:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>SEO title</strong> — <code>[Title] | AILEEN Magazine</code> in the <code>&lt;title&gt;</code> tag</li>
      <li><strong>Meta description</strong> — from <code>metaDescription</code> field, 150-160 chars ideal</li>
      <li><strong>Canonical URL</strong> — deterministic, on every page</li>
      <li><strong>Open Graph tags</strong> — og:title, og:description, og:image, og:url, og:site_name</li>
      <li><strong>Twitter card tags</strong> — summary_large_image format</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Structured data (JSON-LD)</h3>
    <table class="admin-table" style="margin: 1.5rem 0 2rem;">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Schema Type</th><th>Where It Appears</th><th>What It Does</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>WebSite</code></td><td>Every page (via Base layout)</td><td>Identifies the site to Google, enables sitelinks</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>BlogPosting</code></td><td>Every article</td><td>Headline, description, author, dates, publisher</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>Recipe</code></td><td>Posts with <code>contentType: "recipe"</code></td><td>Recipe schema for rich results in search</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>BreadcrumbList</code></td><td>Every article</td><td>Breadcrumb trail in search results</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>FAQPage</code></td><td>Posts with FAQ sections</td><td>FAQ rich results / featured snippets</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h3>XML sitemap</h3>
    <p>Auto-generated at build time. Lists all published pages. Submitted to Google Search Console.</p>

    <h3>Robots.txt</h3>
    <p>Allows crawl of all public content. Blocks admin/preview paths.</p>

    <h3>Canonical URLs</h3>
    <p>Every page has a <code>&lt;link rel="canonical"&gt;</code> tag pointing to its definitive URL at <code>cafecito-ai.com/magazine/...</code>. Prevents duplicate content issues.</p>

    <h3>Image SEO</h3>
    <p>Every image supports <code>alt</code> text through the <code>imageAlt</code> field. Hero images use <code>loading="eager"</code> for above-the-fold rendering. Grid images use <code>loading="lazy"</code>.</p>

    <h3>SEO Dashboard</h3>
    <p>The <a href={`${base}/admin/seo/`}>SEO Dashboard</a> runs 7 automated checks on every post: missing meta descriptions, thin content (&lt;500 words), missing keywords in titles, keyword in intro, H2 keyword coverage, internal link count, and image alt text. Fix what's red.</p>

