    <!-- 10. MONETIZATION -->
    <h2 id="monetization">10. Monetization Surfaces</h2>

    <p>Monetization is built into the content models, not bolted on after the fact. Every relevant post type has commerce surfaces that feel editorial, not pushy.</p>

    <h3>Affiliate products</h3>
    <p>Add a <code>products</code> array to frontmatter for a "Shop the Edit" section. Each product shows name, brand, price, and a link. Best for style guides, The Edit posts, and recipe cookware recommendations.</p>
    <pre><code>products:
  - name: "The Row Margaux Bag"
    brand: "The Row"
    price: "$3,890"
    url: "https://..."
    image: "https://..."</code></pre>

    <h3>Hotel booking CTAs</h3>
    <p>Add <code>bookingLinks</code> for hotel booking buttons. Best for hotel reviews and travel guides.</p>
    <pre><code>bookingLinks:
  - name: "The Breakers Palm Beach"
    platform: "Hotels.com"
    url: "https://..."</code></pre>

    <h3>Restaurant reservation CTAs</h3>
    <p>Add <code>reservationLinks</code> for reservation buttons. Best for restaurant guides.</p>
    <pre><code>reservationLinks:
  - name: "Makoto"
    platform: "Resy"
    url: "https://resy.com/..."</code></pre>

    <h3>Affiliate disclosure</h3>
    <p>Set <code>affiliateDisclosure: true</code> on any post with affiliate links. Shows a tasteful FTC-compliant disclosure above the content.</p>

    <h3>Click tracking</h3>
    <p>Every outbound affiliate, booking, and reservation click fires a GA4 event with the click type and destination URL. This means you can see exactly which links earn revenue.</p>

    <h3>Priority monetizable pages</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Where to stay guides (booking links)</li>
      <li>Hotel roundups (booking links)</li>
      <li>Style shopping guides (product affiliate links)</li>
      <li>Product edits / The Edit (product affiliate links)</li>
      <li>Restaurant guides (reservation links)</li>
      <li>Recipes with cookware recommendations (product affiliate links)</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Ad readiness</h3>
    <p>Templates are designed with future display ad insertion in mind. Content width and paragraph rhythm can accommodate in-content ad units. The 680px article body creates natural ad break points. When you hit 50K sessions and qualify for Mediavine, ads can be added without layout surgery.</p>

    <h3>Monetization Dashboard</h3>
    <p>The <a href={`${base}/admin/monetization/`}>Monetization Dashboard</a> shows which posts have affiliate links, booking CTAs, and reservation CTAs — and which posts are missing revenue opportunities.</p>

