    <!-- 16. EDITORIAL WORKFLOW -->
    <h2 id="editorial-workflow">16. Editorial Workflow</h2>

    <h3>Publishing a new post</h3>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Plan</strong> — Run <code>aileen plan</code> to see keyword-driven post suggestions, or choose your own topic</li>
      <li><strong>Write</strong> — Run <code>aileen write</code> for an AI draft, or write directly in markdown. Save to <code>output/drafts/your-slug.md</code></li>
      <li><strong>Check voice</strong> — Run <code>aileen voice-check output/drafts/your-slug.md</code>. Aim for 75+.</li>
      <li><strong>Edit</strong> — Review the draft. Add your personal experience, real details, specific recommendations. The AI provides structure; you provide soul.</li>
      <li><strong>Deploy</strong> — Run <code>aileen deploy your-slug</code> to copy it to the site's content directory</li>
      <li><strong>Review</strong> — Run <code>npm run build</code> locally to preview, or deploy as draft first with <code>--draft</code></li>
      <li><strong>Publish</strong> — Run <code>aileen publish</code> to build and push live to Cloudflare</li>
      <li><strong>Distribute</strong> — Run <code>aileen pins</code> for Pinterest, <code>aileen social</code> for Instagram/TikTok</li>
    </ol>

    <h3>Refreshing an existing post</h3>
    <ol>
      <li>Run <code>aileen refresh src/content/posts/travel/your-post.md</code> for specific suggestions</li>
      <li>Update the content in the markdown file</li>
      <li>Set <code>updatedDate</code> in frontmatter to today's date</li>
      <li>Run <code>aileen publish</code> to push the update live</li>
    </ol>

    <h3>Required fields before publishing</h3>
    <p>The build will fail if any of these are missing or invalid:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><code>title</code>, <code>metaDescription</code>, <code>targetKeyword</code></li>
      <li><code>pillar</code> (must be travel, style, recipes, or lifestyle)</li>
      <li><code>date</code>, <code>image</code>, <code>imageAlt</code>, <code>excerpt</code></li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Editorial quality checklist</h3>
    <p>Before publishing, every post should pass these questions:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Does it have a clear search intent it's serving?</li>
      <li>Is it part of a destination or topic cluster?</li>
      <li>Does it link to at least 2-3 other posts on the site?</li>
      <li>Does it include original perspective or firsthand experience?</li>
      <li>Does it include at least one conversion path (newsletter CTA, affiliate link, booking link)?</li>
      <li>Does the voice score pass 75+?</li>
    </ul>

    <hr style="border: none; border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); margin: 3rem 0;" />

    <!-- 17. CONTENT STRATEGY -->
    <h2 id="content-strategy">17. Content Strategy</h2>

    <p>The platform supports a cluster-based publishing model. Every post belongs to a cluster — either a destination or a topic — and strengthens the others around it.</p>

    <h3>Core clusters (initial priorities)</h3>
    <table class="admin-table" style="margin: 1.5rem 0 2rem;">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Cluster</th><th>Content types to build</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><strong>Miami</strong></td><td>Best restaurants, where to stay, travel guide, what to wear, date night spots, brunch guide</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Palm Beach</strong></td><td>Best restaurants, where to stay, travel guide, what to wear, romantic restaurants</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>New York</strong></td><td>Best restaurants, where to stay, travel guide, what to wear, neighborhood guides</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Boston / New England</strong></td><td>Travel guide, best restaurants, where to stay, what to wear, weekend itineraries</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Maine</strong></td><td>Bar Harbor guide, best restaurants, where to stay, summer travel guide</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Aspen / Colorado</strong></td><td>Travel guide, where to stay, best restaurants, what to wear (winter), aprés-ski guide</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h3>Content archetypes</h3>
    <p>These are the repeatable formats the system is built to produce efficiently:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Best restaurants in [city]</li>
      <li>Best brunch in [city]</li>
      <li>Best date night restaurants in [city]</li>
      <li>Travel guide to [destination]</li>
      <li>2 days in [city] / weekend itinerary</li>
      <li>Where to stay in [city]</li>
      <li>Best luxury hotels in [city]</li>
      <li>What to wear in [destination] in [season]</li>
      <li>Quiet luxury / capsule / brand edit pages</li>
      <li>Core recipe pages</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Pillar balance</h3>
    <p>Aim for roughly 40% travel, 25% style, 20% recipes, 15% lifestyle. Travel has the highest search volume and monetization potential. Style has the best affiliate revenue. Recipes have strong engagement and Recipe schema advantages. Lifestyle builds personal brand.</p>

    <h3>Cornerstone content</h3>
    <p>Use <code>featured: true</code> and <code>featuredOrder</code> to pin cornerstone content on the homepage. The strongest evergreen pages should remain visible even after newer posts go live.</p>

    <hr style="border: none; border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); margin: 3rem 0;" />

